index 7643c33ef764f0d51b661fdd3892ff813f29e2f4..ac40a2ecba9abb83e51b9a6e407d5b5155271084 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -12,4 +12,13 @@ literal `~` and `/` characters. Invalid syntax and unresolved paths throw errors
 including the nonexistent array element `-`. Pass a plain pointer string, rather
 than a URI fragment such as `#/items/0`. The document is not modified.
 
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` applies an array of JSON Patch operations as defined
+in [RFC 6902](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902.html). It supports `add`,
+`remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, and `test`, in order, and returns an independent
+result without modifying the document or patch values. For example,
+`applyPatch({ items: ["first"] }, [{ op: "add", path: "/items/-", value: "second" }])`
+returns `{ items: ["first", "second"] }`. Invalid patches, unresolved paths, and
+failed tests throw errors. An empty path targets the whole document; removing
+the root returns `undefined`, and a subsequent root `add` can restore it.
+
 Run the tests with `npm test` (Node.js 22.18 or later, with native TypeScript support).
